# Task: focus a Hyprland window by selector, such as class:firefox.
# Program: this file.
# Run: execute docs/recipes/desktop-focus-window.program --input selector=class:firefox
# Test with fakes: put a fake `hyprctl` earlier on PATH that prints its arguments one per
#   line and exits 0. Expect the arguments dispatch, focuswindow, class:firefox.
#   Then make the fake exit 1 and expect the message and a failing exit.
# Explain: the program prints nothing on success; the focus happens in the compositor.
# Replaces (Bash): hyprctl dispatch focuswindow "$1"
# Limit: this recipe does not launch the app when no window matches. Launching is a
#   separate effectful program.
accept selector as text
run "hyprctl" with arguments ["dispatch", "focuswindow", selector] and keep status as code
if code is not 0
  run "printf" with arguments ["focus failed for %s (status %s)\n", selector, code]
  run "false"
